    text: "Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-29: all-status searches for @sentry/node 10.72.0 and Sentry dependency refreshes found the closed packed-consumer lineage pm-fb0lkg and older refresh items, but no item owns 10.72.0. Live pnpm outdated identifies 10.72.0 as the sole compatible candidate; npm-package-arg 14 and TypeScript 7 remain separately owned by pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b."
  - created_at: "2026-08-29T17:47:56.651Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Acceptance observation: focused Sentry/package tests and exact repository coverage passed, but the first live best-effort gate failed closed on PM-CLI-39. Full live event inspection mapped it to canonical host-fault umbrella pm-3lhth4 and the already-delivered v2026.8.28 raw-tar replacement. The latest event was from release 2026.8.21 and no current-release event exists; the stale group will be resolved with recurrence reopening preserved, then the identical linked command rerun."
    edited_at: "2026-08-29T18:01:51.561Z"
  - created_at: "2026-08-29T17:52:03.037Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation evidence 2026-08-29: official @sentry/node 10.72.0 supports Node >=18 and preserves the exported Node declaration surface PM consumes. The resolved graph contains only Sentry 10.72.0 runtime packages and removes the prior @apm-js-collab transformer/tracing-hooks, meriyah, astring, semifies, and source-map production chain. TDD red proved the 10.72 ratchet failed against 10.71 before the update. Green proof: 92 focused tests; 8,124 full tests at exact statements 60,169/60,169, branches 45,397/45,397, functions 12,514/12,514, lines 57,939/57,939; packed artifact; strict TypeScript/npx package smoke across 13 packages; fresh-directory npx and bunx both returned 2026.8.28; zero npm audit vulnerabilities; Sentry critical=0/high=0 and telemetry error rate 1.6% with zero missing error codes. pnpm outdated now leaves only canonical incompatible majors npm-package-arg 14 (pm-ksr40d) and TypeScript 7 (pm-do5b)."
  - created_at: "2026-08-29T18:00:04.253Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Graph-gate correction: the first static-quality run passed typecheck, ESLint, both jscpd zero-clone scans, changelog reproducibility, and the substantive SDK/CLI assurances, then correctly blocked because two newly introduced generic related edges exceeded the ratcheted ceiling and created one prose-edge mismatch. Replaced both generic edges with verifies: this item proves that adopting Sentry 10.72 leaves the separately owned npm-package-arg 14 and TypeScript 7 deferrals intact."
  - created_at: "2026-08-29T18:16:29.893Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final local-quality evidence 2026-08-29: after restoring both typed compatibility-deferral verification edges, the complete non-interactive pnpm lint suite passed. ESLint reported zero warnings, both jscpd scans reported zero clones, repository-static-quality and every SDK/CLI contract/parity/token/refusal gate passed, graph-composition returned prose-edge-gaps exactly at its 1,343 ceiling and record-integrity passed across 56,714 append-only history events. This supplements the already-recorded 8,124-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, packed SDK, npx/bunx, audit, Sentry, and telemetry evidence."
